  "id": "Compound::DB08868 - Gene::1903",
  "verbalization": "Fingolimod is known to bind to S1pr4, a receptor involved in the regulation of sphingosine-1-phosphate (S1P) signaling. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with S1pr4 participating in multiple pathways that ultimately involve S1pr3. The evidence suggests that S1pr4, through its involvement in S1P receptor activity and lysosphingolipid receptor pathways, is linked to S1pr3. This implies that Fingolimod may influence S1pr3 through a mechanism involving S1P signaling, potentially modulating receptor activity or downstream cellular processes. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Fingolimod in regulating S1pr3 through S1P receptor pathways, although the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a functional link between Fingolimod and S1pr3, mediated through S1pr4 and its associated pathways.",
